@@ -1132,6 +1132,11 @@ math:ExactApproximateConflation
     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/math> ;
     rdfs:label "Exact–Approximate Conflation"@x-gmeow-english ;
     skos:definition "The failure raised when a math:ApproximateValue fails to keep an approximation distinct from the exact value — it does not name, through math:approximates, the exact number it stands in for, or does not declare its math:approximationError. An exact number and an approximation of it are distinct objects."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    skos:scopeNote "This class describes a failure of approximation framing. Its current math:ApproximateValue-level report annotation can also classify target-type or count findings; the class alone proves neither resource-identity conflation nor the validity of a numerical error bound."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    skos:example "A math:ApproximateValue that names an exact one-third target through math:approximates but omits math:approximationError illustrates the missing-bound case. Read the finding's component and source shape before identifying that case from a report."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:useWhen "Use when interpreting findings attributed to the canonical math:ApproximateValue restrictions on its exact target and the presence of a numeric error bound."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating this class as proof of an incorrect numerical value, a negative bound, mismatched literal and declared datatypes, or equality between the approximation and target resources; the current restriction group establishes none of those numerical or identity judgments."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:howToUse "Inspect the component, path, value and source shape, then repair the reported obligation: retain a separate math:ApproximateValue, one justified math:Number target through math:approximates and a numeric absolute math:approximationError bound. Validation derives from the existing logic restrictions; establish the bound's numerical justification separately."@x-gmeow-english ;
     gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
 
 math:ConstantAsDecimalLiteral
@@ -1140,6 +1145,11 @@ math:ConstantAsDecimalLiteral
     rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/math> ;
     rdfs:label "Constant as Decimal Literal"@x-gmeow-english ;
     skos:definition "The failure raised when a math:MathematicalConstant is given as a decimal literal — it carries a raw math:quantityValue directly instead of being an exact individual. A constant's decimal expansion belongs to a distinct math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates it."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    skos:scopeNote "The named constant keeps its exact identity independently of any numerical representation. The current math:MathematicalConstant-level report annotation also covers its isExact obligations, so this class alone does not establish that a quantityValue literal was present."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    skos:example "A math:MathematicalConstant with math:isExact true and a direct math:quantityValue of 3.14159 typed as xsd:double illustrates the forbidden-literal case. A justified numerical evaluation belongs on a separate math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates the constant."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:useWhen "Use when interpreting findings associated with the existing constant-local exactness or absence-of-direct-literal obligations while preserving the exact named individual."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid changing the constant's exact identity because an evaluation is rounded, limiting the literal prohibition to xsd:decimal because of this class's label, or inferring a particular violation component from the class alone."@x-gmeow-english ;
+    gmeow:howToUse "Read the reported component, path, value and source shape. Remove a direct math:quantityValue literal from the constant when present, retain math:isExact true, and keep any justified evaluation and numeric absolute error bound on a separate math:ApproximateValue. Repair the actual reported obligation without replacing the canonical constant identity."@x-gmeow-english ;
     gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .
 
 math:StringOnlyMemberCondition
@@ -12975,13 +12985,11 @@ math:ApproximateValue rdfs:subClassOf
     [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty math:approximationError ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange [ logic:unionOf ( xsd:decimal xsd:double xsd:float ) ] ] ;
